      // (USING expression) for table push_subscriptions" — a push
      // subscription endpoint belongs to one physical browser installation,
      // not to a person. Jimmy tests many different accounts on the same
      // phone/browser, so the SAME endpoint often already has a row saved
      // under a DIFFERENT earlier test account. The direct upsert below
      // then tries to UPDATE that other account's row, which RLS correctly
      // blocks ("own push subscriptions" only lets you touch rows where
      // user_id = you). Routed through a SECURITY DEFINER RPC
      // (save_push_subscription, see supabase_push_notifications.sql) that
      // clears out any stale row for this endpoint under a different
      // account first, then saves it under whoever's actually logged in
